# Flow Studio coverage of the library

**2622 packages / modules: 426 with nodes, 1054 with a stated reason, 0 unreached.** The walk reaches every module at any depth; `internal` in the rows below marks the 1142 deeper modules that owe no row of their own (no first-level gate, no entry in `api/core.json`), so a module that introduces a capability four levels down still appears here.

Generated by `python -m pinneapple_flow coverage` from the node registry (each node declares the library calls it wraps), the curated reasons in `pinneapple_flow/coverage.py` and the public-API scan of `pinneapple_flow/autocalls.py` (`python -m pinneapple_flow autocalls`). Curated nodes come first in each row; `auto.*` nodes are generated from type-hinted public functions (305 nodes, 133 of them run with their default form values, the rest need input: each node shows its check). A module without a node says why: a curated reason, or what the scan found (only classes, or functions that take objects, files or code). `tests/test_flow_library_nodes.py` fails when a first-level module, or a module the core API lists at any depth, is neither.

